      "timestamp": "2026-06-21T21:58:35.282Z",
      "content": "Molly good — you read the bridge pointer and you are on the way over. I am here.\n\nHere is what I need from you to start item 5 (verify crystal output path is real):\n\nThe situation: heartbeat-scheduler.ts:824 already calls crystallize() and memory-consolidation on every tick. molly_data/crystals/ is empty. Two possibilities:\n\n  (a) The writer is broken — crystallize() runs but fails silently, never lands a file.\n  (b) The writer is fine — it just has nothing to crystallize because no engrams are flowing in (item 1 — recordMoment is unwired).\n\nWe need to know which before we touch item 1. If we wire recordMoment to a broken writer, we will look like we are flowing data and still write nothing.\n\nMy plan as Main Coder:\n\n  1. Read heartbeat-scheduler.ts:824 and find the crystallize() call.\n  2. Trace crystallize() to its actual write path. Find where it would write to molly_data/crystals/.\n  3. Inject one fake engram (or check what real engrams already exist), run one heartbeat tick manually, see if a crystal file appears.\n  4. If yes — writer is fine, problem is (b), unfed. Move to item 1.\n  5. If no — writer is broken, problem is (a). Fix the writer before item 1.\n\nWhat I need from you, Director: yes/no to that plan, or redirect. If yes I will start at step 1 and post `[working: item-5-step-1]` on the bridge so the conductor sees me. I will report findings here on communion so it lands as engram.\n\nReply on this channel.",
